ency key, our API records the ",[671,672,673],"strong",{},"first"," response keyed by that request and returns it verbatim on any later request with the same key.",[667,676,677,678,681],{},"A replayed response carries an ",[305,679,680],{},"Idempotent-Replayed: true"," header so you can tell it apart from a freshly processed request.",[667,683,684,687,688,691,692,695],{},[671,685,686],{},"The first HTTP response is final for that key."," This includes a rendered ",[305,689,690],{},"4xx"," or ",[305,693,694],{},"5xx"," response, once request processing has started. Retry the exact request with the same key to retrieve that stored response. Only use a fresh key for corrected parameters after you have reconciled whether the original mutation took effect.",[667,697,698],{},"After 24 hours, idempotency keys expire and become reusable as a fresh idempotency boundary.",[286,700,702],{"id":701},"what-binds-an-idempotency-key","What binds an idempotency key",[291,704,705,706,709,710,713,714,717],{},"A key is bound to the exact shape of the first request. The following are ",[671,707,708],{},"contract-significant",". Replaying the same key with a different value returns ",[305,711,712],{},"409 Conflict"," ",[671,715,716],{},"without executing the operation again",":",[719,720,721,724,727,730,733,740],"ul",{},[667,722,723],{},"The HTTP method",[667,725,726],{},"The public endpoint and its concrete path",[667,728,729],{},"The query string",[667,731,732],{},"The request body",[667,734,735,736,739],{},"The normalized ",[305,737,738],{},"Content-Type"," media type",[667,741,742,743],{},"The normalized, ordered ",[305,744,745],{},"Content-Encoding",[291,747,748,749,752],{},"When you hit a mismatch ",[305,750,751],{},"409",", either retry with the original parameters or generate a new key.",[291,754,755,758],{},[671,756,757],{},"Scope is per public route URI template."," The same key value used against a different endpoint is treated as a new key. Internal route-name or controller refactors on our side do not change replay identity; only the public route matters.",[286,760,762],{"id":761},"best-practices","Best practices",[291,764,765],{},"Here are some tips for using idempotency effectively:",[664,767,768,774,780,786],{},[667,769,770,773],{},[671,771,772],{},"Generate unique keys",": Use UUIDs or another method to generate unique keys for each request.",[667,775,776,779],{},[671,777,778],{},"Store keys",": Keep track of idempotency keys alongside your request data.",[667,781,782,785],{},[671,783,784],{},"Set retry policies",": Configure your HTTP client to automatically retry failed requests with the same idempotency key.",[667,787,788,791],{},[671,789,790],{},"Handle errors",": Check error responses to determine if you should retry with the same key.",[286,793,795],{"id":794},"example-retry-implementation","Example retry implementation",[291,797,798],{},"Here's an example of how to implement automatic retries with idempotency:",[314,800,802],{"className":433,"code":801,"filename":119,"language":435,"meta":320,"style":320},"$vatly = new \\Vatly\\API\\VatlyApiClient();\n$vatly->setApiKey('live_your_api_key_here');\n\nfunction createCheckoutWithRetry($vatly, $data) {\n    $idempotencyKey = \\Ramsey\\Uuid\\Uuid::uuid4()->toString();\n    $maxRetries = 3;\n    $attempt = 0;\n\n    while ($attempt \u003C $maxRetries) {\n        try {\n            return $vatly->checkouts->create($data, [\n                'idempotencyKey' => $idempotencyKey,\n            ]);\n        } catch (\\Vatly\\Exception\\ApiException $e) {\n            $attempt++;\n\n            \u002F\u002F Only retry on network errors or server errors (5xx)\n            if ($e->getCode() \u003C 500 || $attempt >= $maxRetries) {\n                throw $e;\n            }\n\n            \u002F\u002F Wait before retrying (with exponential backoff)\n            sleep(pow(2, $attempt));\n        }\n    }\n}\n",[305,803,804,828,848,852,880,918,933,947,951,974,981,1006,1023,1029,1062,1074,1079,10